<title>POLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP POOL B RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP POOL B RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KATOWICE, Poland 1997-04-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of world</p>
<p>championship pool B ice hockey matches on Sunday:</p>
<p> Kazachstan   6    Denmark    4  (3-2 1-0 2-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Kazachstan - Anatoliy Filatov 15, 16, Igor Dorokhin 8,</p>
<p>Vladimir Zavyalov 31, Vadim Glovatskiy 41, Andrey Raiskiy 47.</p>
<p>Denmark - Struve Larsen 5, Broeng Duus 18, Berggren</p>
<p>Thomsen 43, Lars Oxholm 60.</p>
<p> Belarus   6     Austria    4  (1-0 5-0 0-4)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Belarus - Evgueni Rochtchin 22, 39, Alexandre Tsyplakov 8,</p>
<p>Andrei Kovalev 31, Oleg Antonenko 35, Viktor Karatchoun 39.</p>
<p>Austria - Simon Wheeldon 45, 49, 56, Patrick Pilloni 44.</p>
<p> Netherlands  3    Poland    1  (1-0 0-1 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Netherlands - Martinus Rison 5, 59, Thomas Hartogs 57.</p>
<p>Poland - Dariusz Lyszczarczyk 38.</p>
<p> Britain    2     Switzerland   3</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Britain - Paul Adey 40, Richard Strachan 42.</p>
<p>Switzerland - Gian-Marco Crameri 16, Andreas Naeser 27,</p>
<p>Philippe Marquis 37.</p>
<p>Pool B standings:</p>
<p>			  P    W    D    L    F    A    Pts</p>
<p> 1. Belarus	   6    6    0    0   42   19    12</p>
<p> 2. Kazachstan	6    4    1    1   26   18     9</p>
<p> 3. Switzerland     6    3    1    2   24   19     7</p>
<p> 4. Austria	   6    2    2    2   20   20     6</p>
<p> 5. Britain	   6    2    1    3   26   16     5</p>
<p> 6. Netherlands     6    2    1    3   18   33     5</p>
<p> 7. Poland	    6    1    2    3   14   22     4</p>
<p> 8. Denmark	   6    0    0    6   17   39     0</p>
